                <pb facs="0811" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg717"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Williams.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Competitor</hi> case. Did American citizens have fair
                    trial, with opportunity to summon and examine witnesses, and to be defended by
                    counsel of their own selection, and with all other legal guarantees.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
